The word budget is the real constraint. The pass added ~700 words of substance and I paid for all of it by cutting duplication — the draft sits at **4498 of 4500**. It has zero headroom, so anything an editor pass wants to add has to displace something. The one thing I'd restore first is the Charlene/Marliss beat, compressed from a paragraph to a sentence purely to make room.

